62770,ELE-MR-1010,bhavesh2,LineBotz Robot Kit,LineBotz Robot Kit,0.200,39.950,0,, <EOL>* LineBOTZ follows a track YOU create.<br /> <EOL>* Sensors enable LineBOTZ to follow a black line drawn by a felt tipped pen.<br /> <EOL>* Not for children under 3 years,,0,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,52036,Discontinued Products,,30.760,,Friday 21 January 2011 06:55:45 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,,19.950,0,N,43,"Elenco Electronics, Inc."
64571,ELE-MM-8000K,anwar,Micro-Master Computer Training Kit,Micro-Master Computer Training Kit,5,183.250,0,," <EOL>* Starting from scratch, you build a complete computer system.<br /> <EOL>* Our Micro-Master Trainer teaches you to write into RAMs, ROMs, and run an 8085 microprocessor.<br /> <EOL>* You will write the initial instructions in permanent memory in a 2816E2PROM. Teaches all about input and output ports and computer timers.<br /> <EOL>* Complete with 128 page lesson manual, instructions, and experiments.",,10000,3,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,12404,Elenco Electronics/Electronics Division/Computer Based Trainers,,137.740,,Thursday 10 February 2011 10:41:26 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,,109.950,0,N,43,"Elenco Electronics, Inc."
63016,ELE-OWI-979K,bhavesh2,Moon Walker Ii Soldering Sound Sensor,Moon Walker Ii Soldering Sound Sensor,0.200,57.250,0,," <EOL>* Not one, but two!<br /> <EOL>* Light and Sound!<br /> <EOL>* MOON WALKER II has combined the technology of two sensors.<br /> <EOL>* A whimsical indication of future trends, MOON WALKER II begins to walk when it detects a change in light intensity or sound commands.<br /> <EOL>* MOON WALKER II continues it's four legged voyage until instructed by an internal timer to stop.<br /> <EOL>* This kit presents an engaging oppor-tunity to learn about some of the mechanics, operation and history of robots.<br /> <EOL>* When assembled, this robot uses a phototransistor to sense changes in light (such as turning on a lamp) and a condenser microphone to sense changes in sound (such as clapping). It converts those stimuli into electronic signals to power a motor, and MOON WALKER II will walk forward for a preset time.<br /> <EOL>* When it stops, affecting other change in light area light or sound may activate it again.<br /> <EOL>* The sensors be adjusted for different sensitivity levels.<br /> <EOL>* Not for children under 3 years<br /><br> <EOL><b>Specifications:</b><br> <EOL>* Movement: 2 legs on each side by crank shaft.<br> <EOL>* Control: (1)Sound sensor including condenser microphone/transistor; (2)Light sensor/photo-transistor.<br> <EOL>* Power Source: ""AA"" x 1 (not included).<br> <EOL>* Power Consumption: Approx. 210mA.<br> <EOL>* Size: H130 x Diameter 100mm.<br> <EOL>* (PCB Unassembled) - Soldering Required<br> <EOL>* Requires 1 ""AA"" Battery (part # 590001)",,0,1,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,52036,Discontinued Products,,52.740,,Saturday 22 January 2011 07:31:27 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,,0,0,N,43,"Elenco Electronics, Inc."
62828,ELE-MV-979,bhavesh2,Moon Walker II: Light & Sound Sensor,Moon Walker II: Light & Sound Sensor,0.200,53.500,0,," <EOL>* Not one, but two!<br /> <EOL>* Light and Sound!<br /> <EOL>* MOON WALKER II has combined the technology of two sensors.<br /> <EOL>* A whimsical indication of future trends, MOON WALKER II begins to walk when it detects a change in light intensity or sound commands.<br /> <EOL>* MOON WALKER II continues it's four legged voyage until instructed by an internal timer to stop.<br /> <EOL>* This kit presents an engaging oppor-tunity to learn about some of the mechanics, operation and history of robots.<br /> <EOL>* When assembled, this robot uses a phototransistor to sense changes in light (such as turning on a lamp) and a condenser microphone to sense changes in sound (such as clapping). It converts those stimuli into electronic signals to power a motor, and MOON WALKER II will walk forward for a preset time.<br /> <EOL>* When it stops, affecting other change in light area light or sound may activate it again.<br /> <EOL>* The sensors can be adjusted for different sensitivity levels.<br /> <EOL>* Not for Children under 3 years<br /><br> <EOL><b>Specifications:</b><br> <EOL>* Movement: 2 legs on each side by crank shaft.<br> <EOL>Control: (1)Sound sensor including condenser microphone/transistor; (2)Light sensor/photo-transistor.<br> <EOL>* Power Source: ""AA"" x 1 (not included).<br> <EOL>* Power Consumption: Approx. 210mA.<br> <EOL>* Size: H130 x Diameter 100mm.",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,52036,Discontinued Products,,49.340,,Friday 21 January 2011 08:39:15 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,092087699796,32.250,0,N,43,"Elenco Electronics, Inc."
64587,ELE-TCT-355,anwar,Multi-Network Cable Tester,Multi-Network Cable Tester,0.500,41.500,0,," <EOL>* The TCT-355 Cable Tester is a convenient instrument for testing different shielded/unshielded wiring schemed communication cables with RJ-11 and RJ-45 connectors and coax cables.<br /> <EOL>* This tester can be used for testing cables before and/or after they are installed.<br /> <EOL>* Testing status is indicated by multiple LEDs.<br /> <EOL>* Soft vinyl case provides storage for the tester, remote and terminator.",,10000,0,Y,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,12405,Elenco Electronics/Electronics Division/Datacom Testers,,32.310,,Friday 11 February 2011 05:01:47 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,,24.950,0,N,43,"Elenco Electronics, Inc."
62960,ELE-OWI-RETC,bhavesh2,Owi Teachkit,Owi Teachkit,0.200,82.250,0,," <EOL>* A complete teacher resource written by teachers for student experimentation with all OWIKIT robots (except 007 Arm)! Capture student's interest in simple and advanced robotics.<br /> <EOL>* Solve problems, test, measure and record data.<br /> <EOL>* Includes mini-units on the theory of robotics and basic electricity.<br /> <EOL>* Over 110 pages long, complete with answer keys, appendix, and teacher guides in 3-ring binder.<br /> <EOL>* A great value for a photocopy site license.<br /> <EOL>* A complete robotics curriculum featuring OWIKIT Robots of all three levels!<br /> <EOL>* Reproducible and ready for immediate use in your classroom, lab or shop.<br /> <EOL>* Involve your students in familiarzation and problem solving activities in the exciting area of Robotics Technology.<br /> <EOL>* OWIKIT offers ysou the most economical and varied educational robots available,combined with the Robotics Technology Currriculum, a complete learning system is created.<br /> <EOL>* Features Economical : Purchase includes copyright site license to reproduce all materials for classroom use.<br /> <EOL>* Re-ordering of workbooks eliminated!<br /> <EOL>* Flexible : The copyright site license permits the teacher to design and implement a ""custom"" robotics curriculum.<br /> <EOL>* Balanced : Includes a variety of informational and practical resources.<br /> <EOL>* Up-To-Date : Information on current robot research and applications.<br /> <EOL>* Contents Teacher Familiarization Philosophical Background Robotics Technology Concepts 5 Programmed Learning Modules with Test Robot activities for each of the current OWI Robots (information, procedure, data, extra credit and questions sections) Research assignments Appendices: Facts & Tables.<br /> <EOL>* 150 pages.",,0,0,N,0.010,N,Y,1,0,0,0,1000,Y,52036,Discontinued Products,,75.400,,Saturday 22 January 2011 06:06:30 AM,0,0,0.600,"2,3,4,6,8,12",0,309,,0,0,N,43,"E